# UI Components

Reuse primitives from `@/components/ui` and `@/components/animations`. Never re-create a button, link, heading, section or image wrapper inline.

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Primary / secondary CTA | `<Button>` / `<Button variant="secondary">`; over photos `variant="light"` |
| "Discover more →" | `<Link variant="luxury">` |
| Page/section rhythm & surface | `<Section tone spacing textured>` + `<Container size>` |
| Eyebrow + title + description | `<SectionHeading eyebrow title description size as>` |
| Photography | `<ImageWrapper ratio overlay zoomOnHover reveal shape>` |
| Entrances | `Reveal`, `FadeIn`, `Stagger`/`StaggerItem`, `TextReveal`, `ImageReveal`, `SlowScale` |
| "Book your stay" CTA | `<Button onClick={() => openBooking()}>` via `useBooking()` — opens the shared booking panel |
| Quantity input | `<Stepper>` |
| Tiny uppercase facts with hairline dividers | `<MetaList items label>` |
| "01 / 06 —— Label" index line | `<IndexLabel index total label>` |
| Photo that links somewhere (hover zoom + arrow chip, or overlaid caption as children) | `<LinkedImage src alt to ratio>` |
| Different crop on mobile | `<ImageWrapper position mobilePosition>` (mobile applies below `md`) |
| Room photography / room caption | `<RoomImage>` + `<RoomDetails>` from `@/components/hotel/rooms` (`headingAs="h2"` where rooms are the page's main sections) |
| "Every stay includes" band | `<StayIncludes>` from `@/components/hotel/rooms/StayIncludes` |
| Crossfading photographs driven by a selection | Stack every frame absolutely and toggle opacity (see `MomentSequence` in `HomeMoment`) — frames preload, so there is no blank flash; keep `AnimatePresence` for the text beside it |
| Reserve a specific room | `openBooking({ room: slug })` — a bare `openBooking()` always means "any room" |
| Link to a pre-filled contact message | `${routes.contact}?enquiry=<topic>` — topics live in `enquiryTopics` (`@/data/contact`); a room slug or `rooms` means a stay |
| Link into the reservation page with choices filled in | `bookingPath({ checkIn, checkOut, guests, rooms, room, offer })`; the live engine is set once in `bookingEngine` (`@/data/booking`) — null sends an email request instead |
| Hairline that draws in on scroll | `<Divider reveal>` (vertical: `orientation="vertical"`) |
| Muted gold separator (sparingly — one short rule per caption at most) | `<span aria-hidden className="h-px w-10 bg-gold/70" />` |
| Service hours row / typographic menu page | `<DiningServices>`, `<MenuPreview>` from `@/components/hotel/dining` |
| Location / surroundings map | `<DestinationMap destinations activeId>` from `@/components/hotel/destination/DestinationMap` — abstract, data-driven (travel-time rings + bearings), always labelled illustrative; never embed Google Maps |
| Offer entry (index, kicker, title, inclusions, price, link) | `<OfferDetails>` from `@/components/hotel/offers/OfferDetails` — list it editorially (hairline-separated rows), never as cards |
| Experience photography / caption / category filter | `<ExperienceImage>`, `<ExperienceCaption>`, `<ExperienceFilterBar>` from `@/components/hotel/experiences` |
| Photo bleeding off one edge, copy on the 12-col grid | `grid-editorial-bleed` + `col-full` / `col-content` / `lg:col-[1/8]` (line 1 = viewport edge, column n starts at line n + 1) |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded colours, ad-hoc button, rounded card
<div className="rounded-xl bg-[#17352B] p-6 shadow-lg">
  <button className="bg-black px-4 py-2 text-white">Book</button>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — tokens, primitives, tone-aware
<Section tone="forest" spacing="md">
  <Container>
    <SectionHeading eyebrow="Stay" title="Rooms & Suites" />
    <Button to={routes.booking} variant="light">Book your stay</Button>
  </Container>
</Section>
```

- Routes come from `@/lib/routes`; content from typed data in `@/data`.
- Headings: visual size (`size`) is independent of semantic level (`as`) — keep one `h1` per page.
- Register any new font-size/shadow/aspect token in `src/lib/cn.ts` so `cn()` merges it correctly.

## Navigation / masthead

- The masthead (announcement bar + nav) reads the tone of the section beneath it from `data-tone`; put `data-nav-tone="dark"` on full-bleed photographic sections.
- Pages opening with a full-bleed hero set `handle: { headerTheme: 'overlay' }` and pad hero content with `pt-masthead`; all other pages get `pt-masthead` automatically.
- Never animate height to `'auto'` with Framer in persistent chrome (header, bars) — its measurement resets window scroll and cancels smooth scrolling. Transition between fixed tokens in CSS instead.
- Type set directly on photography: a scrim first (`scrim-hero`, `overlay=…`), optionally `text-legible` for a faint halo — never a heavy text shadow.
- Navigation items live in `@/data/navigation` (`navLeft`, `navRight`, `menuNav`) — never hardcode links in the header.
